{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"submission\":\"update.json\",\"summary\":\"Sourced the leader-side consequence the store-failure account had left inferred: on a successful AppendEntries response the replication loop sets that peer's nextIndex one past the accepted entry and records the peer's match index in the leader's commitment, whose match set is built from voters only, so the accepted entry above the gap is counted as replicated for that peer and that range is never sent again. Added two source anchors (replication.go 655-661, commitment.go 35-62) and a behavior knowledge entry with its conditions and anchors. Validation returned valid with those effects and no execution requested; what remains unmeasured in that account is a live leader's own sequence - which request shape its nextIndex produces first and whether anything closes the gap before a snapshot or a restart.\"}"}}
